Research Foundation", "channel_url": "https://rumble.com/c/VaccineSafetyResearchFoundation", "duration": 5178, "uploader": "Vaccine Safety Research Foundation", "live_status": "not_live", "webpage_url": "https://rumble.com/v76c95i-vsrf-live-216-journalism-without-fear.html", "webpage_url_basename": "v76c95i-vsrf-live-216-journalism-without-fear.html", "webpage_url_domain": "rumble.com", "extractor": "RumbleEmbed", "extractor_key": "RumbleEmbed", "view_count": 4257, "like_count": 100, "dislike_count": 0, "description": "Donations are tax deductible and we need your support to continue our work. Text-to-donate, text VSRF to 53555.Show more This week on VSRF Live, we are joined by Sharyl Attkisson — Emmy Award–winning investigative journalist and host of Full Measure, the nationally syndicated program dedicated to original reporting and accountability journalism.\nOver a decades-long career at CBS News, PBS, and CNN, Attkisson has built a reputation for rigorous, fact-driven reporting — and for examining how narratives are shaped inside major institutions. Her work consistently explores media influence, censorship trends, and conflicts of interest in public policy.\nShe is also the author of several bestselling books, including her most recent, Follow the Science, which investigates the influence of pharmaceutical companies on media, scientific discourse, and public health policy.\nIn this episode, we’ll discuss:\n• The current state of investigative journalism\n• How stories are advanced — or sidelined — in major newsrooms\n• Media coverage of high-stakes health issues\n• What “journalism without fear” requires in today’s climate\nWe’ll also be joined by Michael Kane, Director of Advocacy at Children’s Health Defense, to discuss the Covid Justice Resolution and what supporters can do to make their voices heard.\nSign the Resolution at www.covidjustice.org\nJoin us for a focused conversation on accountability, transparency, and the future of independent reporting in a 